	(text "Pads marked [C6]/[C3] differ between the two modules (D15, D18).\nEverything essential uses pads that work on both; BTN2 and GPIO_A/B work\nonly with a C6. SW2 is BOOT and BTN1 (IO9 strap). IO8/IO9 must be high at reset.\nC17/C18 close to module pin 3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 337.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "29f99904-713d-5c36-a0c6-6c7aed6ea714")
	)
	(text "SENSOR PORTS: I2C, OLED, GPIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254.6553 196.725 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2a80774e-d2bb-52ea-816f-7cf75c6e8667")
	)
	(text "TCA9534 pins start as inputs; the 100k pull-downs then hold every valve off until\nfirmware drives them. Address 0x20 (A0-A2 low). P0-P7 high = valve 1-8 on.\nValves 5-8 may be left unfitted (FET, pull-down, diode, LED, resistor, terminal) (D75).\nValves: 12 V DC, low-side switched, up to ~2 A each (D73); total from 12 V IN ~3 A,\nset by F1 (D77). Not for latching valves or 24 V AC valves.\nFLYBACK (D69): each diode returns to the same +12V as its valve's V+ pin, after D2.\nA valve wired to any other supply loses its clamp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.85 530.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4349c4f8-6895-5bf1-9c0e-caea236d427b")
	)
	(text "RS485 (DIRECTION FROM TX)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 372.5839 196.725 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4b2f3f6f-ad34-5246-a022-301c96582a3d")
	)
	(text "DI is tied low: the driver only ever sends 0, gated by TX through Q9.\nA 1 (and idle) is held by the 680R bias pair. Fine for Modbus at 9600 baud;\nmarginal with termination at both cable ends (D21). Bridge JP3 at a bus end.\nTransceiver, bias and pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so RS485 is off with the rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 401.32 307.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "59358297-de3a-5298-8751-a3e77550aeb5")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C6 / C3 MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.5783 196.725 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "66c2ad78-f22b-562e-bd1f-db5b7125c521")
	)
	(text "F1 (3 A hold, 16 V) trips on a shorted cable (D77); D2 (SS54, 5 A) blocks reverse\npolarity; D3 (SMAJ15A) clamps surges. 15 V max input.\nV12_SENSE = 12 V x 100k/660k: 2.27 V at 15 V, inside the ADC range (D23).\nAP63205: fixed 5 V out. L1/C6/C7 to be checked against the datasheet (D25)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.14 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "997512aa-302f-5be2-b7d1-07d04bbba820")
	)
	(text "D7 + Q2: with 5 V present VSYS comes through D7 and Q2 is off;\nwithout it Q2 turns on and the cell feeds VSYS. The charger never carries the load.\nVBAT_SENSE = VBAT / 2 (1M/1M, ~2 uA). RAIL_EN low (default, R21) = both rails off.\n+5V_SW only exists while USB or 12 V is present (no boost from the cell).\nU5 RT9080 (D88): 600 mA, 2 uA quiescent.\nTP1-TP9: probe pads on every supply rail and GND (D89); the silkscreen names the rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 655.32 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a1ada06d-d5f8-5c06-a6c6-2e86813e350e")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so nothing back-powers sensors when the rail is off.\nFirmware must switch +3V3_SW on before ANY I2C traffic, including valve changes:\nthe TCA9534 (on always-on 3V3) holds its outputs meanwhile (D20). OLED shares the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 275.59 312.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a4190802-d039-562b-9af6-cf1ad447fc42")
	)
	(text "USB-C INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 22.9973 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b284306b-44a4-5c40-b794-49b902a2f818")
	)
	(text "VALVE DRIVERS (LOW-SIDE MOSFET PER VALVE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.4571 364.365 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bc7083d3-471b-5720-923b-b75bc17cc218")
	)
	(text "CC1/CC2: 5.1k each to GND (USB-C sink, 5 V only).\nFit R3/R4 for an ESP32-C6 module, R5/R6 (DNP) for a C3 module:\nthe two modules have USB on different pads (DECISIONS D15/D19)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45.72 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c71c2f1e-4ded-55b7-ae74-5cedb6c4c7b0")
	)
	(text "LI-ION CHARGER & CELL PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 476.7531 22.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e227912c-508b-507e-b784-24400b0f345b")
	)
	(text "12 V INPUT, PROTECTION & 5 V BUCK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 23.5417 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e2f8ab27-af5b-5fd1-bc91-d010ad2d7a63")
	)
	(text "PROG: I = 1200 / R. 4.7k = 255 mA; bridge JP1 (2.35k) = 510 mA (D12).\nTEMP: JP2 bridged disables the NTC input. For a cell NTC, cut JP2 and fit\nR11 + J3 with values from the TP4056 datasheet (D27).\nJ4 (JST-PH): pin 1 = cell -, pin 2 = cell +. JST-PH polarity is not standardised:\ncheck each cell before connecting (D28).\nXB5353A (D87) sits in the cell's negative lead: board GND is the pack's P-.\nTrips at 4.30 V / 2.4 V, 3 A discharge; C10 at its VDD pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 486.41 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e8553afd-f35e-55ee-9255-b84fbc5ea139")
	)
